### 2026-08-18 - Telegram new-order alerts for store owners (Ultimate+)
Store owners now get a Telegram ping per order, up to 3 recipients (owner + 2 staff). Uses a SECOND platform-owned bot, separate from the admin one (TELEGRAM_ORDERS_BOT_TOKEN, not TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN) -- owner's call, and correct: Telegram allows one webhook per bot, so sharing a token would have hijacked the admin bot. Key constraint driving the design: a bot cannot message a phone number, only a chat that opened it -- so connecting a recipient is a two-step handshake (owner mints a code -> `telegram_link_codes`; person taps `t.me/<bot>?start=<code>` -> `/api/webhooks/telegram` learns their chat_id -> `telegram_recipients`). Chat ids are therefore NEVER client-supplied. New: migration 059, `/api/integrations/telegram` (GET/POST/DELETE/PATCH, Ultimate gate), `/api/webhooks/telegram` (secret-header auth), `TelegramAlertsCard` in Settings -> Notifications, `notifyStoreNewOrder()` awaited at the end of `/api/orders` (awaited, not floating -- serverless kills the process on response). Toggle lives in `stores.settings.notifyTelegramOrders` (absent = on).
BLOCKED ON OWNER: migration 059 RUN (done 2026-08-18). Still needs `TELEGRAM_ORDERS_BOT_TOKEN` + `TELEGRAM_ORDERS_BOT_USERNAME` + `TELEGRAM_ORDERS_WEBHOOK_SECRET` set + `setWebhook` called on the orders bot -- until then the card shows "non disponible". Verified: tsc clean, eslint clean, 368/368 vitest pass (20 new), `next build` OK, live dev server returns 401 on the unauth'd GET. NOT verified end-to-end (needs the migration + a real Telegram tap).

### 2026-08-08 - JSON-safe 500s on all API routes + fixed OrderFormFields lint error
Follow-up on the storefront JSON crash: added outer try/catch → `NextResponse.json({ error: 'Erreur serveur.' }, { status: 500 })` to every API route that had zero error wrapping, so a thrown error can never leak Next.js's plain-text "An error occurred..." body again. Covered 30 handlers: public storefront (`contact`, `storefront/delivery-fees`, `orders/pay`) + auth (`confirm`, `lockout`, `throttle`, `verify-phone/send`) + crons (`abandoned-cart`, `trial-expiring`) + integrations (`delivery`, `payment`, `sheets`, `sms`) + `billing/cancel`, `domain`, `store/theme`, `store/white-label`, `stores/[id]`, `orders/fraud-shield/toggle`, and all 13 super-admin routes. Also fixed the pre-existing `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` error in `OrderFormFields.tsx` by deriving the delivery fee + loading flag at render from a feeKey'd `fee` state written only in async callbacks (sync setState fully removed, plus a `cancelled` guard so a stale wilaya fetch can't overwrite a newer one). Verified: `tsc --noEmit` clean, `eslint --quiet` clean on `src/app/api` + the component, `vitest run` 228/228 pass.

Root cause: a storefront API call that 500s with a plain-text body ("An error occurred while processing your request") hits `res.json()` unguarded → SyntaxError crash in the console / AI modal. Hardened every storefront JSON parse to fall back to null when the body isn't JSON (`res.json().catch(() => null)` + `?.` on accessors): LeadCaptureForm in `LandingPageRenderer.tsx` + all 5 theme landings (Home/Beauty/Car/Sport/Tech), `OrderFormFields.tsx` (order + online-pay payloads), and the dashboard orders page (ship button + AI-scan). Now shows the friendly FR/AR error instead of crashing. tsc clean, eslint clean on changed files (only pre-existing OrderFormFields react-hooks error remains), 228/228 tests pass. Note: also worth adding an outer try/catch → JSON 500 to `/api/orders/ai-scan`, `/api/orders/pay`, `/api/storefront/delivery-fees` so those routes can never leak the plain-text error page.

### 2026-08-04 - Fixed storefront TikTok pixel silently under-reporting purchases
Merchant complaint: orders land in Krenix + Google Sheets but TikTok Events Manager sees zero purchases; Meta works normally. Root cause was in `src/lib/pixel-events.ts`: we only fired `CompletePayment`, but TikTok e-commerce campaigns are also very commonly optimized against `PlaceAnOrder` (TikTok's semantic "customer placed an order" event, the Purchase equivalent for COD markets). Merchants who picked `PlaceAnOrder` in their campaign got zero attributable conversions from Krenix. Fixed by firing BOTH `PlaceAnOrder` and `CompletePayment` on every completed order (deduped via distinct `event_id`s built from the order id), switched the TikTok payload to Pixel v3's nested `contents: [{...}]` shape (kept legacy top-level fields for report backwards-compat), added `identifyForPixels()` with SHA-256-hashed Algerian-format phone for TikTok Advanced Matching so iOS/ITP visitors still attribute, and wired it into `OrderFormFields.tsx` right before `trackPurchase`. Meta pixel intentionally untouched (owner said it's working, and post-init Meta Advanced Matching would need the pixel id re-passed which isn't in scope here). Server-side TikTok Events API not added — separate scope, would need per-store token in `stores.settings`. tsc clean. NOT verifiable in local preview: needs the merchant's live TikTok pixel + Ads Manager; owner should confirm in TikTok Events Manager 24-48h after deploy.

### 2026-08-02 - Fixed section-visibility toggles being ignored on niche themes
Root cause of "unchecking a section doesn't hide it": `isSectionVisible`/`hidden_sections` was only wired into the generic `LandingPageRenderer.tsx` (per the original 2026-08-02 plan's explicit scope). But `ThemedLanding.tsx` dispatches to a bespoke `*Landing.tsx` per niche theme (Beauty/Tech/Sport/Car/Home) whenever the store has one set — those 5 files are byte-identical copies of the generic renderer's body (verified via diff) and never called `isSectionVisible` at all, so toggling had zero effect for any store on a niche theme. Patched all 5 (`themes/{beauty,tech,sport,car,home}/*Landing.tsx`) with the same guards as the generic renderer, via a scripted find/replace (files are CRLF, identical content) rather than 40 manual edits. tsc + eslint clean on all 6 files (only pre-existing warnings).

### 2026-08-02 - Removed Ayor style, hardened photo-preservation prompt, extended section toggles
Removed the 'ayor' copy style entirely (owner changed mind post-launch) from `lib/claude.ts` (type union + FR/AR style briefs) and the `pages/new` wizard (back to 3-style grid). Rewrote `SCENE_PRESERVATION_PREAMBLE` in `lib/landing-photos.ts` to frame Gemini photo generation explicitly as an "edit, not recreate" task with stronger pixel-fidelity wording — merchant had reported AI photos altering the product too much; no test coverage exists for prompt text so this needs a real (paid) generation to confirm improvement, not yet verified live. Discovered the `hidden_sections` section-visibility feature (benefits/social_proof/product_details/urgency toggles in the editor) was already fully shipped from an earlier session today per `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-02-landing-page-generation-controls.md` — owner didn't realize it existed. Extended it with 4 more toggleable placements per owner's "full control, all placements" ask: `trust_bar`, `recent_clients` (Ultimate ticker), `lead_capture` (mini callback form), `sticky_cta` (Pro+ mobile bar) — new `LandingPageSectionKey` values, gated in `LandingPageRenderer.tsx`, added as pills to the editor's existing toggle bar (no new editable content, visibility-only). tsc clean, lint clean (only pre-existing `<img>`/unused-var warnings), landing-sections.test.ts still passes.

### 2026-07-30 - Meta Conversions API Purchase event for platform's own ad account
Implemented per approved spec/plan (docs/superpowers/specs + plans). New `lib/meta-capi.ts`: fire-and-forget `sendPurchaseEvent` (hashed email/phone via Advanced Matching, no click-ID attribution since Krenix's WhatsApp flow uses plain wa.me links not the Cloud API), no-ops until `META_CAPI_ACCESS_TOKEN`/`META_CAPI_PIXEL_ID` are set. Wired into all 3 subscription-confirmation paths (super-admin manual confirm, SlickPay webhook, SlickPay return route) — fires only for `subscriptions`, not `credit_purchases`. 75/75 tests pass, typecheck clean. Branched as feat/meta-capi-purchase-event off fix/mobile-theme-preview-and-basic-photos (its actual parent, NOT main — that branch is still 36 commits ahead of main/unmerged), then fast-forward merged back into it. Not yet verified live — needs owner's real Meta Events Manager token in production.

### 2026-07-30 - Homepage/pricing polish + Chargily second payment provider + Telegram alerts
Fixed: KrenixLogo.tsx wordmark (was blue image, now text matching homepage nav) — fixes it everywhere at once (pricing/dashboard/auth/super-admin all share the component. /pricing: Ultimate now recommended (was Pro); Business badge downgraded from gold "Meilleure valeur" to plain "Le plus complet"; Growth is now self-serve (register directly) while Business/Agency/Enterprise stay Sur Mesure/WhatsApp. Homepage iPhone mockup (PhoneScrollMockup) resized 300→460 screen height to fix stubby proportions. Order-modal "overlap" bug from user's screenshot could NOT be reproduced (built a faithful static repro of the exact JSX/Tailwind, no overlap found at any width) — left unfixed, flagged to user as possibly already-stale/mid-animation-frame.
Added Chargily as a 2nd BYO-key store payment provider alongside SlickPay (migration 041, lib/chargily.ts, provider-aware /api/integrations/payment + orders/pay + store-payment webhook/return, two-provider dashboard UI). Both verified live: Chargily full sandbox checkout+status-poll cycle passed; SlickPay only read-only auth check run (its .env key is LIVE mode — held off on creating a real invoice pending owner confirmation, never got an answer).
Added Telegram alert for auto-confirmed ONLINE platform payments (subscriptions/top-ups paid via SlickPay checkout, not just manual BaridiMob-proof submissions) — `notifyPlatformPaymentConfirmed` gated on `confirmAndActivate`'s idempotent true-return. Discovered the platform-billing SlickPay flow (checkout/webhook/return routes, migration 027, confirmAndActivate) was ALREADY fully built on this branch — the "unmerged feat/slickpay-payments branch" memory was stale, no merge needed. Telegram API itself unreachable from this dev sandbox (network egress blocked) so bot delivery untested here — needs owner to confirm receipt after deploy. Migration 041 not yet run in Supabase by owner. Deployed to production (commit a4ec2d7).

